From 9bd929bf66443c7fd8e25bc2ab1e3eeb2d55dbd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ForkMesh Deploy <deploy@forkmesh.local>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:30:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/18] fix(dashboard): link repository lists to the
 organization address

Repository cards and lists already read "forkmesh/forkmesh" (the logical
owner) while their links pointed at "mirror6/forkmesh" (the machine that
publishes the bytes), so clicking a card left the organization address.

Organization aliases are routable: org_alias_rewrite maps /<org>/<repo> and
every /api/repo/<org>/<repo>/... path onto the serving node, and a direct
visit resolves the alias again on the repo page. So the link can now carry
the label. User identities have no such rewrite, so a repo whose logical
owner is only a user keeps the physical /<node>/<repo> route.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
